(7494187, 1193525, 94815, '<td valign="top">This is such an oddly (for me) captivating piece of what - nostalgia - I think, although I''m not from there nor have ever been there (Dover I guess). The high vantage point and gone horizon line are deliciously modern but the collection of visual elements retain the (carefully constructed) look of the pastoral in olden times - say, 19th century, to pick one. Its a greatly sensitive eye that saw this and fed a mind that responded in that little corner of the retained collective consciousness that we (or some of us) can be made to well up and share if only with ourselves.</td>', 'This is such an oddly (for me) captivating piece of what - nostalgia - I think, although I''m not from there nor have ever been there (Dover I guess). The high vantage point and gone horizon line are deliciously modern but the collection of visual elements retain the (carefully constructed) look of the pastoral in olden times - say, 19th century, to pick one. Its a greatly sensitive eye that saw this and fed a mind that responded in that little corner of the retained collective consciousness that we (or some of us) can be made to well up and share if only with ourselves.', '2017-01-23 22:20:06.000000', NULL, 1),
